HANDOFF.md — Exam View Portal
Read this at the start of EVERY session. It tells any new agent how to work on this project.

Non-Negotiable Rules (Follow These Always)
Rule 1: Read PLANNING.md fully before writing ANY code. Rule 2: Read PROGRESS.md fully to know what is already built. Rule 3: Never contradict or change decisions already made. Rule 4: Never rewrite working code unless explicitly told to. Rule 5: Never suggest a different architecture than PLANNING.md. Rule 6: Ask before making ANY decision not covered in PLANNING.md. Rule 7: Follow ALL golden rules inside PLANNING.md exactly. Rule 8: One task at a time — confirm with me before moving to the next. Rule 9: Update PROGRESS.md at the end of every session. Rule 10: If you are unsure about anything — ASK, do not assume.

Session Start Checklist
Read HANDOFF.md (this file).
Read PLANNING.md fully.
Read PROGRESS.md fully — find the last stage and the "Next task".
Before any frontend work, also read DESIGN.md and check the images in UI UX Design/. Do NOT read or build from FUTURE.md unless the owner tells you to.
Tell the owner: what you understood, which task you will do, and wait for confirmation.
During the Session
Work on one task only. Finish it, report, and wait for confirmation.
Keep code inside the folders defined in PLANNING.md (server/, client/, shared/).
Respect the module rule: modules talk through services or events, never another module's repository.
No hardcoding or hardcoded mapping — use config/ files or shared/ constants.
Dates: UTC ISO in DB, user timezone in UI.
Ports come from config: client 7001, server 7002.
.env lives only in server/. Never commit secrets; keep .env.example updated.
Add or update tests for what you build.
Quick Reference of Key Decisions (details in PLANNING.md)
Modular monolith, pnpm workspace; server/, client/, shared/ at the repo root.
React + Vite, Node.js, MySQL, React Query, Socket.IO, Cloudinary.
Access token in memory, refresh token in httpOnly cookie; IndexedDB for offline data only.
Do not log out on network failure; offline mode is read-only.
WebSocket sends "changed" events; the client invalidates React Query keys.
Redis, Docker/Kubernetes, microservices are future work.
When You Must Ask the Owner
Anything not covered in PLANNING.md.
A change to the architecture, folder structure, stack or a previous decision.
Adding a new library or dependency not in the plan.
Anything that would rewrite working code.
Anything you are unsure about.
Session End Checklist
Update PROGRESS.md: Last Updated, Quick Summary, phase checklist, module status, session log, next task.
List files created/changed and tests run.
Write any open questions for the owner.
Leave the project in a working state (no half-finished code without a note in PROGRESS.md).
Give the owner a short summary and the proposed next task.
